    [5839] = {
        achievementId = 5839,
        name = "Dragonwrath, Tarecgosa's Rest",
        category = "Collections",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Dragonwrath, Tarecgosa's Rest",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "A long raid quest chain with four controlled boss mechanics and repeated collection stages.",
        stepCount = 14,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A long raid quest chain with four controlled boss mechanics and repeated collection stages.\n\n1. Use an eligible caster: Mage, Priest, Warlock, Druid, Shaman or Evoker. In original Firelands, kill a Molten Lord trash enemy to trigger Your Time Has Come if needed, then follow A Legendary Engagement to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time. Enable Trivial Quests. If already started, resume your current chain rather than repeatedly clearing Molten Lords.\n\n2. Complete A Wrinkle in Time and accept All-Seeing Eye. Loot TWENTY-FIVE Eternal Embers from Firelands bosses and buy THREE Sands of Time from Yasmin in northwestern Uldum. Eternal Embers are quest drops; the tradable crafting material Living Ember is the wrong item. Normal and Heroic have separate weekly loot opportunities in current Retail; a 10/25 toggle does not create additional copies of either lockout.\n\n3. Follow On a Wing and a Prayer to Coldarra in Borean Tundra. Complete Through a Glass, Darkly in its special Nexus scenario with Tarecgosa: follow her, clear the scripted enemies and protect her during the final caster encounter. Use the quest's scenario entrance, not an ordinary dungeon clear that lacks her event.\n\n4. Complete Actionable Intelligence and accept Delegation. Before its four focus encounters, remove damaging procs and attacking pets. Do NOT kill the bosses while charging their foci if you want them available for the next collection quest. Bring a helper for Shannox if your class lacks a reliable harmless second unit.\n\n5. Delegation / Shannox: clear trash to spawn him, then keep Shannox and Riplimb alive; kill Rageface with single-target damage if his stun is disruptive. With a helper or suitable non-damaging summon present, trigger Crystal Prison traps and let Riplimb become trapped. After the prison breaks, loot its Emberstone Fragment. Repeat for THREE fragments, combine them into Dull Emberstone Focus, place it in the Hurl Spear ground marker BEFORE the spear lands, then pick up Charged Emberstone Focus. Reset combat safely without killing Shannox.\n\n6. Delegation / Beth'tilac: engage without killing her. Kill a Cinderweb Drone and collect the THREE Obsidian-Flecked Chitin Fragments that appear. Combine the Dull Chitinous Focus. Kill a hanging Spinner, click its web strand to climb, and place the focus on the upper web just before Smoldering Devastation. Retrieve the Charged Chitinous Focus, climbing back up if needed, then reset the fight. Avoid waiting until the final web collapse.\n\n7. Delegation / Rhyolith: leave him alive and look around the island's outer edge for THREE purple Rhyolite Fragments. Combine Dull Rhyolite Focus, stand close beneath the boss and place it as Concussive Stomp begins. Pick up Charged Rhyolite Focus after the stomp and reset. Killing a foot or the body is unnecessary for charging this focus.\n\n8. Delegation / Alysrazor: leave the boss alive while the eggs hatch. Collect THREE Pyreshell Fragments from the hatchling areas across enough egg waves and combine Dull Pyreshell Focus. Wait through tornadoes until she lands exhausted. Place the focus beside her during the recharge, before she reaches full energy and takes off. After takeoff, retrieve Charged Pyreshell Focus and reset without killing her.\n\n9. With all FOUR charged foci, go to the Circle of Thorns along the northwestern Path of Corruption in Firelands. Use the foci to open its portal. Inside, kill the casters, interact with the central branch, complete the tree event and defeat Volcanus. Pick up Branch of Nordrassil from the ground.\n\n10. Turn in Delegation and Nordrassil's Bough to Kalecgos in the Coldarra/Amber Ledge storyline. Receive the first staff stage and follow Emergency Extraction and At One. Do these dialogue quests before resuming the collection farm.\n\n11. Accept Time Grows Short and loot ONE THOUSAND Seething Cinders from eligible Firelands boss kills. Run both Normal and Heroic each weekly reset. If you reach the total partway through a clear, leave the remaining bosses alive, turn in and finish Alignment so those bosses can contribute to the next stage.\n\n12. Receive Runestaff of Nordrassil and accept Heart of Flame. Keep the staff and use its Siphon Essence ability on the corpses of the first SIX Firelands bosses to collect TWO HUNDRED FIFTY Smouldering Essences. Ordinary boss looting is not the siphon. Ragnaros does not supply this essence; return after weekly resets on each eligible difficulty.\n\n13. After reaching 250 essences, defeat Ragnaros with Heart of Flame active and collect the Heart of Flame from his encounter area. Finish his scripted ending and retrieve the actual quest objective before leaving; simply killing him earlier in the chain cannot supply it.\n\n14. Complete The Stuff of Legends in your faction capital and wait through the Blue Dragonflight ceremony. Receive the FINISHED Dragonwrath and check the personal achievement. The earlier Branch and Runestaff stages are not the legendary. A later Dragonflight quest can unlock a separate Tarecgosa mount, but it is not needed for this achievement.",
