    [5858] = {
        achievementId = 5858,
        name = "Bear-ly Made It",
        category = "Dungeons",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Bear-ly Made It",
        difficulty = "easy",
        difficultyReason = "The high-level rescue route is generous once you use the correct legacy dungeon and boss order.",
        stepCount = 4,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - The high-level rescue route is generous once you use the correct legacy dungeon and boss order.\n\n1. In Midnight, visit Zidormi at Thalassian Pass, Eastern Plaguelands 53.8,8.7, and select legacy Quel'Thalas. Travel through the original Ghostlands to Zul'Aman at 81.5,64.4. Set Heroic before entering; the new outdoor Zul'Aman is not this dungeon.\n\n2. Speak to Vol'jin at the entrance and complete the gong interaction without moving to cancel it. When the gate opens and the rescue timer starts, head directly to Akil'zon in the northwest. Defeat him, then continue to Nalorakk in the southwest, clearing the approach packs that make him advance onto his platform. These early bosses add time.\n\n3. Defeat Jan'alai in the southeast, then Halazzi in the northeastern temple, all before the sacrifice timer expires. Mount between pulls when out of combat and avoid unnecessary side bosses or long loot stops.\n\n4. Free the four captives and collect their rewards. After the fourth timely rescue, follow that captive's reward sequence; with this route Kasha breaks vases and leaves the bag containing the Amani Battle Bear. Loot the container rather than assuming the mount is automatically learned. The achievement needs the four rescues, not Malacrass or Daakara.",
