    [5871] = {
        achievementId = 5871,
        name = "Master of the Molten Flow",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Master of the Molten Flow",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Find enemies with the correct abilities and control damage through three distinct mechanics.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Find enemies with the correct abilities and control damage through three distinct mechanics.\n\n1. Finish Mount Hyjal through Aessina's Miracle, then begin the Sanctuary of Malorne's Regrowth/Molten Front introduction. Enable Trivial Quests. Complete The Sanctuary Must Not Fall, collect 20 Marks of the World Tree for Calling for Reinforcements, and follow Through the Gates of Hell into the Molten Front. The portal is at 27.6,56.3 in Hyjal.\n\n2. Recruit the Druids of the Talon for 150 Marks of the World Tree. On their daily route, finish the base quests and escort the druid through Into the Fire into the underground Molten Flow. Follow the tunnel and its exit to the Furnace. Recruiting the Shadow Wardens alone does not open this route.\n\n3. Before fighting, dismiss attacking pets and remove damage procs. Bring Soft Foam Sword for these OUTDOOR enemies to lower health without an accidental kill. Some Flamewakers lack the required special ability: test different spawns rather than waiting indefinitely on the wrong creature.\n\n4. SENTINEL: aggro a Flamewaker Sentinel, lower its health safely and let it pick you or a helper up. Kill it WHILE it is carrying that target. Killing it first, or after it has thrown the carried target away, misses the condition.\n\n5. HUNTER: find one that casts Wild Barrage. Safely lower its health if needed, then keep running in a circle through the ENTIRE barrage without touching its spear landing markers. The criterion is surviving the cast unharmed; do not kill or interrupt it before the channel completes.\n\n6. SHAMAN: near the rear of the cave around 50.0,40.3, find one that casts Flamewave and lower it with Soft Foam Sword. Stand so its own flame wave crosses the shaman. Let THAT damage finish it; do not deliver the killing blow yourself. High-level avoidance can interfere: later Retail reports use repeated /sit while facing away so waves can connect, sometimes after waiting for its mana to run low. This can take several minutes.\n\n7. Inspect each of the three criteria independently. If a hunter never casts or a shaman never loses health to its waves, replace that spawn and retry. No corpse-running shortcut or obsolete class talent is needed to reach the cave or complete the mechanics.",
        stepCount = 7,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 198, x = 0.271, y = 0.625, step = 1, label = "Sanctuary of Malorne - unlocks and daily quests" },
            { mapID = 338, x = 0.47, y = 0.907, step = 2, label = "Malfurion's Breach - campaign hub" },
            {
                mapID = 338,
                x = 0.5,
                y = 0.40299999999999997,
