    [5873] = {
        achievementId = 5873,
        name = "Ready for Raiding II",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Ready for Raiding II",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Five rotating lieutenants and a separate avoidance condition for each.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Five rotating lieutenants and a separate avoidance condition for each.\n\n1. Finish Mount Hyjal through Aessina's Miracle, then begin the Sanctuary of Malorne's Regrowth/Molten Front introduction. Enable Trivial Quests. Complete The Sanctuary Must Not Fall, collect 20 Marks of the World Tree for Calling for Reinforcements, and follow Through the Gates of Hell into the Molten Front. The portal is at 27.6,56.3 in Hyjal.\n\n2. Recruit both campaign branches and complete Calling the Ancients for 125 marks to unlock the dependable Strike at the Heart route. Follow the day's Wardens/Talon quests to its final daily, then speak to Witherbranch at Ragnaros' Reach to activate the visible lieutenant.\n\n3. ANCIENT FIRELORD: move off the Flame Spout ground marker and avoid its sweeping frontal breath. DEVOUT HARBINGER: keep moving away from the pursuing Creeping Inferno; its Ignite effect means the attempt failed. Keep damaging pets out of the forbidden effects as well.\n\n4. ANCIENT SMOLDERING BEHEMOTH: leave the Stomp radius and interrupt or move away from the fire nova. CINDERWEB QUEEN: move out of the large web blast; deal with spawned spiders without standing in the web impact.\n\n5. ANCIENT CHARSCALE: move away from the thrown javelin and the lava-ball landing shadows, then dodge all five successive Line of Fire attacks. Let their full sequence finish without a hit if a quick kill did not award the criterion.\n\n6. High-level quick kills can satisfy the avoidance criteria. If hit, finish the fight, wait for its short respawn and reactivate Witherbranch while your quest allows it. Check the relevant criterion after each clean kill.\n\n7. Inspect the active lieutenant after daily resets. Reports confirm that retaining an unfinished Strike at the Heart can allow later checks, but repeats of the same boss are common; cross-realm hopping is not a reliable way to change the daily selection. Finish today's route again if the retained quest no longer activates the encounter.",
        stepCount = 7,
        waypoints = {
